Snyk CLI code-signing key (backlog #0-147, ADR-0033): signs sha256sums.txt.asc of every Snyk CLI release.
check-pinned-tools.sh trusts a signature only by the key whose fingerprint names this file.
Fingerprint 467717A30B2B4658415975629691DA64D0025194, checked on 2026-10-17 in three places that agree:
docs.snyk.io ("Verifying CLI standalone binaries"), snyk/cli help/_about-this-project/snyk-code-signing-public.pgp
(this copy), keys.openpgp.org. A new Snyk key is a new file, committed after the same three-way check.
The primary key signs (its one subkey, cv25519, is for encryption only); both EXPIRE ON 2027-01-06: from then on
gpg reports every signature by it as EXPKEYSIG and check-pinned-tools.sh fails Lint Workflows on every pull
request and both snyk.yml jobs before the CLI is installed (it warns from 30 days ahead).
Before that date: take the extended key from the snyk/cli repository and keys.openpgp.org, check the
fingerprint against docs.snyk.io again, and replace the armor below (or add a new key's file, if Snyk rotated).
gpg ignores this text before the armor.

